KPL/MYB

Displacement of a point of the Earth's crust by the tides of the solid Earth, the pole tide
and the loads of the ocean tides and of the ocean pole tide, after the IERS Conventions 2010
(IERS Technical Note 36, chapter 7, version of 2018-02-01), read by myb_site_tides_create
(myb/site.h) with the prefix 'IERS10_SITE'.

Sources:
  IERS Conventions 2010, chapter 7, https://iers-conventions.obspm.fr/content/chapter7/icc7.pdf,
    SHA-256 ffe8ffb13c8bbc3b07ac298f458fcbb564974377b165fb93921a05bb0d55043d:
    section 7.1.1 - eq. 5 and 6 (degrees 2 and 3 with the nominal Love and Shida numbers and
    their dependence on the latitude), eq. 8 and 9 (the l(1) terms), eq. 10 and 11 (the
    imaginary parts), eq. 12 and 13 with Tables 7.3a and 7.3b (frequency dependence), eq. 14
    (the permanent part); section 7.1.2 (ocean loading by the admittance of 342 waves);
    section 7.1.4 - eq. 21 (the secular pole) and eq. 26 (the pole tide); section 7.1.5 -
    eq. 29 (the load of the ocean pole tide).
  The rows of the frequency dependence are those of the reference routines STEP2DIU.F
    (SHA-256 898c70d4b8d50e09e0c717c911c4117b3ad1ca4996d369c258b68d00ea3a5674) and STEP2LON.F (SHA-256 f9d3bf0317222986d22e53557020bb13a6fbb90f8e3c9915137da6184d82813a) of
    https://iers-conventions.obspm.fr/content/chapter7/software/dehanttideinel/: 31 diurnal
    rows (29 that are not zero) and 5 zonal ones, of which the tables of the text print the
    11 and 5 largest; the amplitudes are copied without change (K1 out of phase is -0.80 mm
    in the routine and -0.78 in the text).
  The 342 waves of the tide-generating potential (Cartwright, Tayler and Edden) are the
    table of ADMINT.F (SHA-256 478e3f0c001c09dd4d9e2e9920033d29e76eb60b808238e416e6db9ffaeae6c8) of
    https://iers-conventions.obspm.fr/content/chapter7/software/hardisp/, copied without
    change.
  Downloaded on 2026-11-11. Converted by a script that turns Doodson's multipliers into those
  of the Delaunay arguments, theta = m chi - N.F, and checks the 16 rows of the text against
  the Delaunay multipliers printed there.

LOVE = ( h(0) h(2) l(0) l(2) h3 l3 ): h2 = h(0) + h(2) (3 sin^2 phi - 1) / 2 and likewise l2,
  phi the geocentric latitude of the point.
L1 = ( diurnal semidiurnal ): the l(1) of eq. 8 and 9.
IMAGINARY = ( hI lI of the diurnal band, hI lI of the semidiurnal band ), eq. 10 and 11.
RADIUS: the equatorial radius of eq. 5 (m).
PERMANENT = ( H0 ), m: the wave of zero frequency of the potential; its displacement, the
  part of eq. 5 that does not change, is sqrt(5 / (4 pi)) H0 h2 (3 sin^2 phi - 1) / 2 along
  the radius and sqrt(5 / (4 pi)) H0 l2 (3 / 2) sin(2 phi) northwards (eq. 14).
Frequency dependence, over the arguments (chi, l, l', F, D, Omega) of
data/grav/iers2010-tides.tk (chi = GMST + pi; t in Julian centuries of UT1 from J2000.0), in
the form of data/frames/iau2006-cip.tk (columns: power, a_sin, a_cos, the multipliers), mm:
  BAND1_RS = sum dR(ip) sin(theta) + dR(op) cos(theta),
  BAND1_RC = sum dR(ip) cos(theta) - dR(op) sin(theta), BAND1_TS and BAND1_TC likewise
  with dT: at the longitude lambda of the point the sums of eq. 12 over theta + lambda are
  S = RS cos(lambda) + RC sin(lambda), C = RC cos(lambda) - RS sin(lambda);
  BAND0_R = sum dR(ip) cos(theta) + dR(op) sin(theta), BAND0_T likewise (eq. 13).
POLE = ( radial, south, east ) in mm per arcsecond of the wobble (eq. 26):
  radial = POLE[0] sin(2 theta) (m1 cos(lambda) + m2 sin(lambda)),
  south  = POLE[1] cos(2 theta) (m1 cos(lambda) + m2 sin(lambda)),
  east   = POLE[2] cos(theta) (m1 sin(lambda) - m2 cos(lambda)), theta the colatitude,
  m1 = xp - xs, m2 = -(yp - ys). SECULAR_POLE = ( xs0 xs1 ys0 ys1 ) in milliarcseconds:
  xs = xs0 + xs1 (t - 2000), t in Julian years (eq. 21).
OCEAN_POLE = ( G aE rho_w ge Omega GM gamma_R gamma_I ), SI: the load of the ocean pole tide
  is K ((m1 gamma_R + m2 gamma_I) u^R + (m2 gamma_R - m1 gamma_I) u^I), m in radians,
  K = 4 pi G aE rho_w Hp / (3 ge), Hp = sqrt(8 pi / 15) Omega^2 aE^4 / GM (eq. 29), u the six
  coefficients of the point; the constants are those of chapter 1 of the Conventions (the
  test file of the coefficients was made with G = 6.673e-11).
WAVES: rows of Doodson's multipliers (tau s h p N' ps) and the amplitude of the wave in the
  potential. BLQ: the multipliers of the waves whose amplitudes and phases a table of ocean
  loading gives, in the order of its columns (M2 S2 N2 K2 K1 O1 P1 Q1 Mf Mm Ssa).
  WAVE_SHIFT = phases (degrees) added to the argument of the waves of the long-period,
  diurnal and semidiurnal bands. The displacement of a component is
    sum_i H_i Re( Z(f_i) exp(i (theta_i + shift)) ),
  Z the admittance A exp(-i phi) / |H| of the given waves carried to the frequency f_i of
  each wave within its band (myb/site.h).

\begindata

